8.1 Wikipedia user options
==========================

The user option ‘spofy-wikipedia-language’ controls which language
edition of Wikipedia to use.  The default value is ‘"en"’ for the
English Wikipedia.  Set it to another language code (e.g., ‘"de"’,
‘"fr"’, ‘"es"’) to look up articles in that language instead.

   The user option ‘spofy-wikipedia-db-file’ specifies the path to the
SQLite database file for caching lookup results.  The default is
‘spofy-wikipedia.sqlite’ in the user Emacs directory.

   The user option ‘spofy-wikipedia-backend’ specifies the ‘gptel’
backend name to use for classical music lookups (e.g., ‘"Gemini"’ or
‘"Claude"’).  When ‘nil’ (the default), the backend is inferred from
‘spofy-wikipedia-model’ or falls back to the global ‘gptel-backend’.

   The user option ‘spofy-wikipedia-model’ specifies the ‘gptel’ model
for classical music lookups.  When ‘nil’ (the default), it uses the
global ‘gptel-model’.  These two options follow the same resolution
pattern as ‘elfeed-ai.el’: setting the model alone is sufficient if it
uniquely identifies a backend.

   The user option ‘spofy-wikipedia-fallback-to-artist’ controls what
happens when no Wikipedia article is found for the album or musical
work.  When non-nil (the default), Spofy falls back to opening the
artist's Wikipedia page instead.  This is useful because many albums and
classical works lack dedicated Wikipedia articles, while their artists
or composers typically do.  Set it to ‘nil’ to signal an error instead.


